  {
   "text": "{\"sections\":[{\"section\":\"summary\",\"body\":\"On the bank's calculation, Tidewell Medical meets all of its covenants for the period ended October 31, 2026. However, the certificate reports higher unrestricted cash and runway than the bank calculates. The most important change is the narrowing cash cushion: unrestricted cash of {{fact:c71186d0-4532-4650-b75d-ba279b3f1fd5}} against a {{fact:587ac04d-68ab-41c8-acab-61e61e84577d}} floor leaves headroom of {{fact:370f7427-3266-4da7-b8ed-3e2ef5795114}}, down each month. A high-severity open item is waiting for review because the bank statements and the certificate disagree on unrestricted cash, and it needs a reviewer's determination.\"},{\"section\":\"covenants\",\"body\":\"Minimum Unrestricted Cash is met on the bank's calculation: {{fact:c71186d0-4532-4650-b75d-ba279b3f1fd5}} against a required {{fact:587ac04d-68ab-41c8-acab-61e61e84577d}}, a cushion of {{fact:370f7427-3266-4da7-b8ed-3e2ef5795114}}. The certificate reports a higher {{fact:009b0def-8f49-40a4-b70b-ed2fb4ec1f81}}. Minimum Runway is also met: {{fact:5c962657-cdc9-4c76-86e7-d5549a472a92}} months against {{fact:5924794a-483f-4ff7-a304-12c5266711bc}}, a cushion of {{fact:2be480c2-276a-4efa-87fa-e64211c8e831}}. Here too the certificate is higher, at {{fact:bad0b846-4288-4aaa-957d-a5669c9c321f}}. Revenue to Plan is {{fact:c277bd3c-74ac-4e79-b397-8c5931c3ba02}} against a minimum of {{fact:aa19c384-9083-4796-ab5b-79411e86381e}}, a cushion of {{fact:9a38fdcd-b162-4b44-b97a-35e865451eb5}}, and it agrees with the certificate at {{fact:024f36aa-bc1d-4dfb-8d20-278ef760ee0e}}.\"},{\"section\":\"risks\",\"body\":\"The highest-priority item is the open, high-severity mismatch between bank statements and the certificate on unrestricted cash. The certificate's {{fact:009b0def-8f49-40a4-b70b-ed2fb4ec1f81}} exceeds the bank's calculated {{fact:c71186d0-4532-4650-b75d-ba279b3f1fd5}}, so the reviewer should establish which figure is correct. Low-severity signals show unrestricted cash headroom narrowing each month, with a sharp drop to {{fact:370f7427-3266-4da7-b8ed-3e2ef5795114}}. Runway headroom has also fallen to {{fact:2be480c2-276a-4efa-87fa-e64211c8e831}}, most steeply in October. Revenue headroom slipped only marginally, to {{fact:9a38fdcd-b162-4b44-b97a-35e865451eb5}}, which suggests the cash decline reflects spending or working capital rather than weaker sales.\"}]}",
   "type": "text"
  }
